{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Harbonah.</b> Some say that Elijah, may his memory be blessed, appeared to the king in the likeness of a eunuch. The sense of \"and the king's wrath abated\" is that his wrath did not rest until Haman was hanged by decree, and I restored it upon him. And if they are two, [they are] two forms."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:12.322758850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}